      "output": "# Backprop — static review record\n\nScope: static cross-read of the evidence report, the spec and the test report. Nothing here was re-executed; items the reports do not show are marked **not actually run**.\n\n## Spec math vs evidence\nThe spec's engine math follows the evidence and labels inference. Observed-and-matching: matmul dot fwd/bwd, relu/sigmoid/tanh backward, softmax max-trick, crossEntropy = probs−onehot, mse 0.5·sq with (x−y) grad, weight-decay folded into gradient, biases not decayed. Deliberate departures from the convnetjs library are flagged **[inferred]** and justified by evidence of absence/non-standard behaviour: canonical Adam (library inverts bias-correction), AdamW (absent), inverted dropout (library scales at test time), He/Xavier inits (library has only √(1/fan_in)), LayerNorm, embeddings, and schedules — all noted in §2 and the §10 note. Add/sub/mul/div broadcast grads, gelu, logSoftmax, concat/reshape and gradCheck are marked [inferred], consistent with the evidence (no autodiff/tape in library). Verdict: the marking is honest and consistent with the evidence.\n\n## Acceptance checks — what the test report shows\nThe test report lists aggregate counts and names only four failing tests by text; it does **not** map every §8 numbered check to a pass/fail line. So most §8 numbers are **not individually shown** as passing — only the final count.\n\n- Final run: **67/67 tests passed, 18/18 planted caught, 0 page errors, not blank (PASS, exit 0).**\n- Initial run: **63/67, 18/18 planted caught**, with four named failures.\n\nFailing before fixes (by report text, not by §8 number):\n1. tensor `softmax∘matmul + rows sum 1` → maps to **check 6** (ce rel err 0.00188 > 1e-3).\n2. lab `addDense then removeLast restores count` → **check 28**.\n3. lab `sampling temp0 deterministic` → not a numbered §8 check (self-named lab test).\n4. lab `char sample prints vocab chars` → relates to **check 29** (vocab chars).\nFailures 2–4 shared one cause: dataset id `charseq` vs registered `text`.\n\n## Planted failures caught\nReport states **18/18 planted caught both before and after fixes**. The spec §9 lists **11** planted failures; the report counts 18 and does not enumerate which §9 items they are, so the §9→caught mapping is **not actually shown**.\n\n## What the fixes changed\n- tensor: carry the checked loss in float64 (`o._f64`) for crossEntropy/mse/sum(axis=null); `gradCheck` reads it. Analytic grad, stored tensor, eps and 1e-3 bound unchanged.\n- data: added `charseq`→`text` alias in `U.data.get/set/current`. No generator, class count or test expectation changed.\nReport asserts no test, expected value or planted failure was altered.\n\n## Spec parts no check appears to cover\nNot covered by any shown check: schedules `step` and `warmup-cosine` (only cosine/constant tested, #13); optimizers momentum/nesterov/adagrad/rmsprop (only adam #12 and adamw #14); datasets circles/moons/xor/sine/digits (only spiral #15/#17 and blobs #16); layernorm and embedding math; initialisers (he/xavier/embedding scale); L2 weight-decay-in-gradient path; most commands in §3 (≥35) beyond those exercised; dock panels 1–4 (only error-box behaviour #27); light theme and layout breakpoint. These are **not actually run** by any check the report lists.\n\n## Separation note\nThis record is a static review only; the awwo-check-page results above are the test report's claims, not an execution performed here.",
